{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nTier-1 supply-chain + packaging hygiene for the Gerrit **Verified-gate vote path**, with **zero\nadded hot-path latency**. Actions epic 5664 findings S1 (widen zizmor), S2 (make the SHA-pin\nclaim true), and S3 (`twine check` pre-merge). All checks run inside existing steps (`make lint`\nand the already-present `_artifact-probe.yml` build), so no new job and no measurable Verified\nminutes are added.\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThe workflows that actually cast the authoritative `Verified` vote were unaudited and partly\nmispinned:\n\n- **Zizmor audited `release.yml` only** (`Makefile` `RELEASE_WORKFLOW`), so `gerrit-verify.yaml`\n  and every reusable it calls were never checked for pinning / credential-persistence /\n  template-injection issues.\n- **The SHA-pin claim was partly false.** `gerrit-verify.yaml:21` asserts all third-party\n  actions are SHA-pinned. In `gerrit-verify.yaml` itself only `actions/setup-python@v7`\n  (lines 76, 175, 359) was mutable — its `actions/checkout` steps (lines 141, 445) were already\n  pinned. The mutable `actions/checkout@v7` refs lived in the reusables the vote path calls\n  (`_build-and-test.yml`, `_artifact-probe.yml`, `_optionality.yml`, `_eval-discipline.yml`),\n  alongside their mutable `actions/setup-python@v7`. `_mutation.yml` was already fully pinned.\n- **`twine check` ran only at release**, so a packaging-metadata regression could earn\n  `Verified +1` and only fail at publish. The `_artifact-probe.yml` job installs only\n  `pip`+`build`, so a pre-merge `twine check` must install `twine` itself first.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. **S2 (pin):** pin every mutable `actions/checkout@v7` -> `@9c091bb2…  # v7.0.0` and\n   `actions/setup-python@v7` -> `@5fda3b95…  # v7.0.0`, matching the repo's existing pin+comment\n   convention. Coverage: `_build-and-test.yml`, `_artifact-probe.yml`, `_optionality.yml`, and\n   `_eval-discipline.yml` (both action families); `gerrit-verify.yaml` (only its three\n   `setup-python@v7` refs — its checkouts are already pinned). This makes the line-21 claim true.\n2. **Zizmor remediation (surfaced by S1):** add `persist-credentials: false` to the non-pushing\n   branch-head checkouts (the repo's established `artipacked` remedy, already used in\n   `gerrit-verify.yaml`), and route `_mutation.yml`'s `${{ matrix.shard }}` through `env:` to\n   clear the `template-injection` finding — a behaviour-preserving hardening (still exactly one\n   bounded shard per job).\n3. **S1 (widen zizmor):** extend the `make lint` zizmor target from `release.yml` to\n   `release.yml` + `gerrit-verify.yaml` + all five reusables it calls (`_build-and-test.yml`,\n   `_mutation.yml`, `_optionality.yml`, `_artifact-probe.yml`, `_eval-discipline.yml`). Runs\n   inside the existing `make lint` step; no new job.\n4. **S3 (twine):** add a step to `_artifact-probe.yml` right after the existing wheel/sdist build\n   that FIRST installs twine (`python -m pip install --upgrade twine`, since the probe env has\n   only pip+build) and THEN runs `twine check --strict dist/*` (seconds; validates package\n   metadata pre-merge, on both the branch-head and Gerrit-patchset lanes).\n5. Update the `test_ci_workflow_parity.py` `one_matrix_shard` contract so it verifies the shard\n   still flows to exactly one `--shard` from `matrix.shard`, now via `env:` (dataflow preserved).\n\n## Portability\n\nNo new capability is gated on a specific CI provider. Zizmor runs under `make lint`, which is the\nportable, provider-agnostic entry point (offline locally, online in CI) — a checkout with no CI\nprovider still gets the audit by running `make lint`. Pinning and the `env:` change are static\nYAML. `twine check` lives in the artifact-probe job but validates the same `python -m build`\noutput a developer can check locally with `pip install twine && twine check dist/*`.\n\n## Latency\n\nZero measurable Verified hot-path minutes added: S1/S2/zizmor-remediation change files and the\nexisting `make lint` argument set (no new step); S3 adds a seconds-scale check (twine install +\ncheck) to a job that already builds the artifacts.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `make lint`'s zizmor target audits `release.yml` + `gerrit-verify.yaml` + all five\n      reusables it calls, and a full `make lint` passes green (zizmor: no findings).\n- [ ] Every `actions/checkout` / `actions/setup-python` ref across the vote path is SHA-pinned\n      with a `# vX.Y.Z` comment, so `gerrit-verify.yaml`'s line-21 SHA-pin claim is true.\n- [ ] Non-pushing branch-head checkouts on the vote path set `persist-credentials: false`\n      (zizmor `artipacked` clear), and `_mutation.yml` passes `matrix.shard` via `env:`\n      (`template-injection` clear).\n- [ ] `_artifact-probe.yml` installs twine and runs `twine check --strict dist/*` after the\n      build, on both the branch-head and Gerrit-patchset lanes.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` passes, its `one_matrix_shard` contract updated to\n      assert the shard reaches exactly one `--shard` from `matrix.shard` via `env:` (never\n      `--all-shards`).\n- [ ] No new Gerrit Verified hot-path job or measurable added latency."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787762269414988001,"uuid":"4c48329d-0d6c-43b5-baa3-56a5326d19b3"}